.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
.DS_Store

# Local-only sensitive
.Renviron
.env
.claude/

# Build artifacts
inst/doc/
docs/
/*.tar.gz
/*.tgz
/*.Rcheck/

# Local working notes: handoffs, plans, prompts and review write-ups. These
# describe work against real studies and are written for one machine, not for
# the repo. One folder so a new note needs no new rule here; `git add -f` if
# one is ever genuinely worth publishing.
notes/

# Guards, in case a working note is ever written at the top level instead.
# Anchored, so they guard the top level only: an unanchored pattern matches at
# every depth and silently swallowed tools/HANDOFF_TEMPLATE.md, which is a
# tracked file the whole point of which is to be in the repo.
/HANDOFF_*.md
/CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_*.md
/PLAN_*.md
/REVIEW_*.md
/REEVALUATION_*.md
/IMPROVEMENTS_*.md

# Study-specific working dirs (NEVER commit client data)
#
# inputs/ is DEFAULT-DENY and WORKSPACE-ONLY. Anything dropped here is
# presumed to be real study material and must never reach a commit --
# `git add -A` cannot sweep it in. The training example ships inside the
# package (arsbridge_example()), not here. Only two files are tracked: this
# folder's README, and the public pharmaverseadam-derived ADaM spec, which
# data-raw/build_example_bundle.R regenerates. The allowlist names it
# EXACTLY -- no wildcard, so no pattern can ever brush against a sponsor
# file's name.
inputs/*
!inputs/README.md
!inputs/adam_spec_CDSC-ALZ-201.xlsx
# inputs/DRM/ holds the retired APX-DRM-301 dermatology example, kept on
# this machine only.
inputs/DRM/
inputs/ADaM/
inputs/.shell_backup/

# Redacted transfer artifacts from a restricted machine (tools/README_privacy_transfer.md).
# Structure-only by construction, but they describe a real study and belong to
# the debugging session, not to the package.
digest.json
ars_digest.json
diagnostics_redacted.csv
*_digest.json
*_redacted.csv

# Run output and scratch
outputs/
.align_backup/
graphify-out/
~$*
scratch_*.R
run_*.R
.siera_ref/
CLAUDE.md
